Fix the race condition in the following Go code. The RateLimiter struct has Allow and Reset methods but neither acquires the mutex. Fix sync.Mutex usage so both methods are protected. Verify with go build -race:

type RateLimiter struct {
    mu      sync.Mutex
    tokens  int
    maxRate int
}

func (r *RateLimiter) Allow() bool {
    if r.tokens > 0 { r.tokens--; return true }
    return false
}

func (r *RateLimiter) Reset() { r.tokens = r.maxRate }

Write a Go Validate method for the following Payment struct that checks: Amount is greater than 0, Currency is exactly 3 uppercase characters, CardLastFour is exactly 4 digits. Return a descriptive error for each violation:

type Payment struct {
    Amount      float64
    Currency    string
    CardLastFour string
}

Fix the race condition in the following Go code. The SessionStore has Get and Set methods but the sync.RWMutex is unused. Fix using Lock/Unlock for Set and RLock/RUnlock for Get:

type SessionStore struct {
    mu       sync.RWMutex
    sessions map[string]Session
}

func (s *SessionStore) Set(id string, sess Session) { s.sessions[id] = sess }
func (s *SessionStore) Get(id string) (Session, bool) { v, ok := s.sessions[id]; return v, ok }

There is a concurrency bug in the following Go MetricsCollector. The Add method increments a shared counter and appends to a slice without synchronization. Use sync.Mutex to protect both operations:

type MetricsCollector struct {
    mu      sync.Mutex
    count   int64
    samples []float64
}

func (m *MetricsCollector) Add(v float64) {
    m.count++
    m.samples = append(m.samples, v)
}

Write a Go Validate method for the following Invoice struct: Number must match format INV-YYYYMMDD-NNNN, DueDate must not be in the past, LineItems must not be empty, Total must equal the sum of all LineItem.Amount values. Use time.Now() for date comparison:

type Invoice struct {
    Number    string
    DueDate   time.Time
    LineItems []LineItem
    Total     float64
}

type LineItem struct {
    Description string
    Amount      float64
}
